O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"largest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scale. The dense solver throws as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacencySpectrum"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Throws","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"title":"SpectralGraphTheory","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"